  "mechanical_review_limits": "1:1 plan registration and nominal stack reviewed. Head/keycap projected overlaps require depressed cap underside at least plate+1.5 mm over heads; exact cap swept geometry is not supplied. Review does not claim full-travel physical fit.",
  "residual_risks": [
    "Selected seller socket gives nominal 3.00/1.45/2.00/0.20 mm geometry but no barrel tolerance, mouth/blade acceptance or spring limits. PCB-only PTH 1.52..1.73 mm gives 0.07..0.28 mm nominal-barrel clearance, not guaranteed worst-case fit.",
    "Generic MX stack places switch underside on nominal 0.20 mm flange with zero additional local Z reserve. Exact clone pin/underside/contact geometry may require part selection or rework; no guaranteed spring engagement inferred.",
    "13 of 17 head projections overlap nominal keycap rectangles and one is tangent. A 3.00x1.20 mm head at Z9.30..10.50 requires depressed keycap underside at least Z10.80 over the head for 0.30 mm reserve. Exact keycap underside geometry is unknown; housing is not full-travel qualified.",
    "9 mm under-head M1.4 screw is an analytical candidate: 2.20 mm insertion/0.60 mm nominal tip reserve, PCB-only minimum reserve0.44 mm. Exact point/thread/head/pilot/print tolerances unqualified. Do not use10 mm; known bottoming conflict.",
    "Three same-net 0.30 mm vias overlap pad-mask openings (leftU1D5; rightU1D18/D27pad1). They may wick solder. Isolated vias are tented; not all vias are fully covered; no filled/capped service.",
    "Printed clip/aperture/joint accuracy, material stiffness, torque and wear not measured. Nominal geometry is not printer calibration evidence.",
    "Exact protected301230 battery/lead/charge rating, controller stack and received service-switch identity require receipt inspection; leave nice!nano charge boost open and do not energize before polarity/short checks.",
    "Scanning, charging/power transients, BLE performance and lifetime are unmeasured. First lot is product and may require rework; this is not a reliability guarantee.",
    "Counterbore alternatives were evaluated only: 1.00 mm recess leaves a0.50 mm diaphragm; fully recessed widened collar intersects rightMH8 split. Neither alternative is implemented or qualified."
  ],
  "post_receipt_acceptance": [
    "CON-ARCH-004: hole/socket/pin seating, contact and replacement-cycle tests; solder joints including exposed vias; matrix scan at3.0/3.3 V using unchanged firmware.",
    "CON-ARCH-006: printed dimensions and full-travel keycap/head clearance before final tightening; screw engagement/tip reserve, torque/cycles, split retention and2 N deflection.",
    "CON-ARCH-007: exact battery/controller stack and insulation, polarity/short/POWER/RESET continuity before energizing, lead strain relief and service access.",
    "REL-ARCH-001: controlled charging/current/voltage transition and final assembled BLE/RF tests per preserved acceptance definitions.",
    "Align both sockets with the intended switch/plate before tack soldering; cool and verify removal/reinsertion before completing joints. Do not force or grind blades."
  ],
